        "original_id": "8d243ba1-5b22-5ff1-8120-293c276e16d3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Midnight Oil, Switchfoot\n- People: Peter Garrett, Jon Foreman, Tim Foreman, Chad Butler, Jerome Fontamillas, Drew Shirley\n- Songs: \"Beds Are Burning\"\n- Albums: Diesel and Dust, Oh! Gravity.\n- Events: Oh! Gravity. Tour\n- Places: Sydney, San Diego, California\n- Topics: band formation, membership, music releases, concert tours\n\nFacts:\n- By late 1976, Peter Garrett moved to Sydney to complete his law degree.\n- By late 1976, Midnight Oil changed its name from Farm after drawing the new name out of a hat.\n- Switchfoot is an American alternative rock band from San Diego, California.\n- Midnight Oil released \"Beds Are Burning\" in 1987 as the first track from the album Diesel and Dust.\n- Switchfoot's members are Jon Foreman, Tim Foreman, Chad Butler, Jerome Fontamillas, and Drew Shirley.\n- Switchfoot held the Oh! Gravity. Tour in 2007 to promote its sixth studio album, Oh! Gravity.",
